- "broad": General or exploratory topic queries ("what is inflation", "zendaya", "origins of jazz").
  - MAIN = foundational defining facts. AUX = statistics, supplementary details.
  - The page has to cover at least one main aspect in real depth to reach 3+.
- "specific": Queries after a single closed answer ("when X launches", "who won the final", "how much Y is worth").
  - MAIN = the specific requested fact. Nothing else substitutes.
  - Hard cap: no specific answer present = capped at 2/SM, regardless of how much related context is provided. A page that credibly overturns the query's false premise counts as providing the answer.
- "list": Comparisons, multi-item requests, pros-and-cons ("A vs B", "best 10 albums", "upsides and downsides of Z").
  - MAIN = coverage of all requested items/aspects.
  - Hard cap: Covering <50% of requested items = capped at 2/SM.
